[36m== DEMONSTRATED[0m
The live foreign-eBPF gate attack was executed against the two real
daemons, not a synthetic batch. The probe holds no key; the collector,
in a different process and holding the only signing key, signed
IntegrityUnknown and withdrew attested coverage. The attack was not
prevented -- a CAP_BPF adversary can blind the sensor -- but it could
not make the system report a clean window it could not justify.

The attested batches were then verified OFFLINE by a separate process
given two files and the published public key -- no collector, no socket,
no passphrase -- and the same verifier refused the same archive with one
record deleted. That is the Phase 1 exit gate, end to end.
